  "name": "cqrs-es",
  "description": "A lightweight and opinionated Rust framework for implementing Command Query Responsibility Segregation (CQRS) and Event Sourcing, specifically optimized for serverless architectures. It provides a robust set of abstractions for domain aggregates, event streams, and asynchronous command handling while maintaining strict separation between write and read models. The system features a pluggable persistence layer with built-in support for PostgreSQL, MySQL, DynamoDB, and SQLite, alongside sophisticated event upcasting and replay capabilities.",
